  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Ever since the recent live build, proximity contacts (like flex contacts on avatars with biceps) randomly flicker from 0.0 to 1.0 despite the actual proximity. This was not a problem before the constraint update. I have checked with the contact overlay to make sure the contacts were isolated from other avatars and it was still flickering. The behavior is random and only lasts for 15 seconds before happening to another avatar. \n\nExtra things to note:\n\n- This still happens to contacts with \"Allow Others\" disabled\n\n- Happens only to one receiver contact at a time (usually)\n\n- Affected contacts are typically always driven (like a bicep contact)\n\n- Contacts are not tied to any constraints\n\n- Reproduction? : Be in any populated instance with plenty of proximity contacts",
